How the Library evaluates AI tools
The AI functionality embedded in our subscribed databases and systems is tested by our
Library Generative AI working group to ensure it aligns with Murdoch University's AI Acceptable
Use guidelines and is appropriate for teaching, learning and research purposes.
We have designed an assessment rubric that rigorously tests the tool or functionality against
several categories of criteria:
Functionality: accuracy, ease of use, transparency, reliability, relevancy;
Accessibility: compliance with accessibility standards, cost of use;
Technical: operating systems and browser requirements, additional download requirements,
administrative workload;
Privacy, data protection, and rights: authentication, user control over data;
Ethics: bias and fairness, copyright considerations, ethics of parent company, energy
efficiency.

